<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea to absorb 800 bln won through repos.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea to absorb 800 bln won through repos.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea said on Thursday it has decided to absorb 800 billion won from the banking system repurchase agreements (repos), maturing on May 19.  </p>
<p>A central bank official said the measure was decided to siphon off excessive short-term market liquidity.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the central bank absorbs 800 billion won today, we don't expect tightening of liquidity at the banking system,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
